## Where the hyphenation engine came from

The hyphenation engine in this package is a Dart
implementation of the hyphenation algorithm of
[the legacy engine](https://github.com/the legacy engine), whose authors offer it
under a GPL 2.0 / LGPL 2.1 / MPL 1.1-or-later tri-license.

**The MPL branch of that grant is elected here, at version 2.0.** MPL 2.0
applies per file, and the four files that carry the algorithm say so in their
own header:

- `lib/src/hyphenation/patterns.dart`
- `lib/src/hyphenation/pattern_trie.dart`
- `lib/src/hyphenation/parser.dart`
- `lib/src/hyphenation/matcher.dart`

Everything else — the widgets, the line breaker, the caches, the rest of
`lib/src/hyphenation/`, the tests and the benchmarks — is covered by the MIT
license above. The full MPL 2.0 text, and what it asks of you if you
redistribute those four files, is in
[THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md](./THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md).

The hyphenation dictionary (`hyph_*.dic`) is **not** bundled with this
package; you supply your own, and it carries its own license.
